{"id":"10b43f4fd4ac0d83","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-thm-projective-determinacy-strength.md","title":"PD Consistency Strength","display":"thm-projective-determinacy-strength — PD Consistency Strength","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-projective-determinacy-strength","aliases":["58-thm-projective-determinacy-strength","PD Consistency Strength"],"display":"thm-projective-determinacy-strength — PD Consistency Strength","depends_on":["[[58-df-woodin]]","[[58-df-determinacy]]","[[58-df-projective-hierarchy]]","[[58-df-consistency]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-projective-determinacy-strength"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-projective-determinacy-strength</span><span>PD Consistency Strength</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-projective-determinacy-strength — PD Consistency Strength"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"da3159c0c219916e\" href=\"?note=da3159c0c219916e\" title=\"58-df-woodin\">58-df-woodin</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4cc4baec9297fd1e\" href=\"?note=4cc4baec9297fd1e\" title=\"58-df-determinacy\">58-df-determinacy</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d4ac523055965e48\" href=\"?note=d4ac523055965e48\" title=\"58-df-projective-hierarchy\">58-df-projective-hierarchy</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"6996aaff4caeacce\" href=\"?note=6996aaff4caeacce\" title=\"58-df-consistency\">58-df-consistency</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal N=\\omega^\\omega\">\\(\\mathcal N=\\omega^\\omega\\)</span> is Baire space and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_n^1(\\mathcal N)\">\\(\\Sigma_n^1(\\mathcal N)\\)</span> is the boldface projective pointclass from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d4ac523055965e48\" href=\"?note=d4ac523055965e48\" title=\"58-df-projective-hierarchy\">58-df-projective-hierarchy</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T_{\\mathcal N}=\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}\">\\(T_{\\mathcal N}=\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}\\)</span> is the full tree of finite plays with move set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\">\\(\\omega\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Det}(T,A,M)\">\\(\\mathrm{Det}(T,A,M)\\)</span> is the exact three-argument determinacy predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"4cc4baec9297fd1e\" href=\"?note=4cc4baec9297fd1e\" title=\"58-df-determinacy\">58-df-determinacy</a> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Woodin}\">\\(\\mathrm{Woodin}\\)</span> is the Woodin-cardinal predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"da3159c0c219916e\" href=\"?note=da3159c0c219916e\" title=\"58-df-woodin\">58-df-woodin</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Con}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Con}_S\\)</span> is syntactic consistency from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"6996aaff4caeacce\" href=\"?note=6996aaff4caeacce\" title=\"58-df-consistency\">58-df-consistency</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\)</span> is the fixed first-order ZFC axiom theory and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PD}\">\\(\\mathrm{PD}\\)</span> is the projective-determinacy sentence defined below.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vartheta_n\">\\(\\vartheta_n\\)</span> is the first-order set-theory sentence displayed below.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}determinacy\\text{-}definition}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PD}\\coloneqq\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\forall A\\in\\Sigma_n^1(\\mathcal N)\\;\n\\mathrm{Det}(\\omega^{&lt;\\omega},A,\\omega)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}determinacy\\text{-}definition}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PD}\\coloneqq\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\forall A\\in\\Sigma_n^1(\\mathcal N)\\;\n\\mathrm{Det}(\\omega^{&lt;\\omega},A,\\omega)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}determinacy\\text{-}finite\\text{-}woodins}\\vdash\n\\vartheta_n\\coloneqq\n\\ulcorner\\exists\\delta_0\\cdots\\exists\\delta_{n-1}\\;(\n\\delta_0&lt;\\cdots&lt;\\delta_{n-1}\\land\\bigwedge_{i&lt;n}\\mathrm{Woodin}(\\delta_i))\\urcorner,\n\\qquad\nT_{&lt;\\omega\\mathrm W}\\coloneqq\\mathrm{ZFC}\\cup\\{\\vartheta_n:n\\in\\omega\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}determinacy\\text{-}finite\\text{-}woodins}\\vdash\n\\vartheta_n\\coloneqq\n\\ulcorner\\exists\\delta_0\\cdots\\exists\\delta_{n-1}\\;(\n\\delta_0&lt;\\cdots&lt;\\delta_{n-1}\\land\\bigwedge_{i&lt;n}\\mathrm{Woodin}(\\delta_i))\\urcorner,\n\\qquad\nT_{&lt;\\omega\\mathrm W}\\coloneqq\\mathrm{ZFC}\\cup\\{\\vartheta_n:n\\in\\omega\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}determinacy\\text{-}strength}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Con}_S(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\cup\\{\\ulcorner\\mathrm{PD}\\urcorner\\})\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Con}_S(T_{&lt;\\omega\\mathrm W})\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}projective\\text{-}determinacy\\text{-}strength}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Con}_S(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\cup\\{\\ulcorner\\mathrm{PD}\\urcorner\\})\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Con}_S(T_{&lt;\\omega\\mathrm W})\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The right-hand theory is a first-order scheme: for each standard finite <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> it asserts at least <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> Woodin cardinals. It does not assert that a set coding an omega-sequence of Woodin cardinals exists.</li>\n<li>The definition of PD now supplies the play tree, payoff set, and move set required by the registered determinacy predicate.</li>\n<li>Infinitely many Woodin cardinals give the upper-bound proof of projective determinacy; reverse inner-model results recover every finite Woodin-mouse consistency level from PD.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Martin and Steel, A Proof of Projective Determinacy, Journal of the American Mathematical Society 2 (1989)</li>\n<li>Steel, Projectively Well-Ordered Inner Models, Annals of Pure and Applied Logic 74 (1995)</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-woodin","status":"resolved","id":"da3159c0c219916e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-woodin]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-determinacy","status":"resolved","id":"4cc4baec9297fd1e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-determinacy]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-projective-hierarchy","status":"resolved","id":"d4ac523055965e48","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-projective-hierarchy]]","embed":false},{"target"